{"id": "EUVD-2026-53784", "enisaUuid": "a75a0875-f892-3770-8915-562561ad46d8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix double-free in SMB2_close() replay\n\nA response-bearing attempt can return a replayable error and free its\nresponse buffer. If SMB2_close_init() fails before the next send, cleanup\nretains the previous buffer type and frees that response again.\n\nReset response bookkeeping before each attempt to prevent the stale free.", "datePublished": "2026-08-06T07:13:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:48:43", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/037511726228aaf165c7067ff2bfc88eaecdf1f3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0aa97edf7c347c0f54e7e60c4740574b8120c66a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d15d83125007f673aec4323e1bbbaaffbe87ea13", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b18ed621dbfceecea5539848cddcb9272c9a61e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f96e1cdcb63ed3321142ff2fcdf784e32cda8fee"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64597", "GHSA-4vgx-hp6g-jmm8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.36, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e820779-47bc-37bb-a86a-2e5569424f78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "179ef90b-f465-3144-8eb7-f4bf8981f6d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <f96e1cdcb63ed3321142ff2fcdf784e32cda8fee"}, {"id": "372285b7-ee31-39e7-9a82-9162ec3e14fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.39"}, {"id": "5bc981ab-043b-3ee7-bd0c-72433c139598", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <b18ed621dbfceecea5539848cddcb9272c9a61e1"}, {"id": "6e63f9c9-5afa-303e-a93d-8a8385718b01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"